.TH EUCLID-CLI-EAG-LIST-ROUTES 1 "September 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eag-list-routes \- list the configured gateway routes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli eag list-routes
.RB [ \-\-prefix | \-p
.IR PATH ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists the configured routes with their paths, the applications behind
them, what they require of a caller, and whether they are in service.
.PP
Inactive routes are listed too. They are configuration that exists but
is not being served, and leaving them out would make a route somebody
deactivated look deleted.
.PP
This shows what is
.IR configured ,
not what is
.IR reachable :
a route whose application has no running instance is listed exactly like
any other and answers 503. Use
.BR euclid-cli-emm (1)
to see how many instances an application currently has.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-prefix " " \fIPATH\fR
Only routes whose path starts with this. Omit for all of them.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The call succeeded, including when it matched nothing. The routes are
printed as JSON.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid arguments, no administrator session, or the server rejected the
request.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli eag list-routes
euclid-cli eag list-routes --prefix /resource
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eag (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eag-get-route (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eag-create-route (1),
.BR euclid-cli-emm (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Jens Vogt <jens.vogt@opitz-consulting.com>
